{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/input/archive.test.ts@L102","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/input/archive.test.ts","span":{"start":102,"end":110}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/input/archive.test.ts","span":{"start":102,"end":110},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:2eaf361c466334ec3738402b360c46e567f1bad92879a2e0339d707938504e88","meta":{"text":"Build a STORED (method 0) ZIP with FULL control over per-entry central-directory metadata — method,\nflags, declared compressed/uncompressed sizes, and external attributes — so a test can craft the\nadversarial shapes yauzl must reject at emit time WITHOUT allocating the declared expanded sizes.\nyauzl emits each entry from the central directory BEFORE reading its local header (validateEntrySizes\nruns in openReadStream, which a rejected entry never reaches), so a central directory that claims a\n100 MiB+1 entry, a symlink mode, or an encrypted flag triggers extractArchive's validate() at the\n`entry` event and is rejected before any byte of the (absent) payload is read. The local header is\nwritten with the SAME sizes/method/flags as the central record so a passing entry's stream is sound."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/input/archive.test.ts@L16","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/input/archive.test.ts","span":{"start":16,"end":16}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/input/archive.test.ts","span":{"start":16,"end":16},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:82dc95ae48cd1745a8f193403fbc02efddd102ca10e1a7214cfeadf2e73d2057","meta":{"text":"Build an in-memory ZIP from {path, data} entries via yazl (deflated, realistic)."}}
{"id":"expl:packages/pipeline/src/input/archive.test.ts@L28","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"packages/pipeline/src/input/archive.test.ts","span":{"start":28,"end":30}},"file":"packages/pipeline/src/input/archive.test.ts","span":{"start":28,"end":30},"lang":"typescript","hash":"blake3:9028328a390756c07db9dee1e33cb5ed20f435c30ef4869a8b149c3259b7be0b","meta":{"text":"Build a ZIP from STORED (uncompressed) entries with FULL control over entry names — so the test\ncan craft names yazl refuses to build (traversal, trailing-slash dirs). Minimal hand-rolled ZIP:\nlocal headers + data + central directory + EOCD."}}
{"id":"expl:scripts/ifhash-check.mjs@L54","kind":"explanation","commentRef":{"file":"scripts/ifhash-check.mjs","span":{"start":54,"end":58}},"file":"scripts/ifhash-check.mjs","span":{"start":54,"end":58},"lang":"javascript","hash":"blake3:97626c54d81d747497cc95782f8206e8d9d82a07c6213046a9f0f096afc19d38","meta":{"text":"Build a soul with a real source file + caller/callee edges so context/source carry a non-trivial\nbody. assess calls helper; handle calls assess → context surfaces callers + callees + a body. The\nassess body is deliberately long (a multi-line risk computation) so the rehydrated source is ~3 KB\n— the realistic migration-analyst case the \"measurably drops\" gate is about (a 99-byte stub vs a\nmulti-KB body, not a 99-byte stub vs a 400-byte skeleton)."}}
